{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/961120-rage-across-texas","id":961120,"title":"Rage Across Texas?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-31T10:57:30-07:00","id":961120,"title":"Rage Across Texas?","content":"after watching preacher (AMC) and re reading the comic book. i felt like doing a modern cowboy tale within the universe of werewolf, been thinking about ST a game set in texas, any advices about caerns, pentex, feras and other kins?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T11:41:58-07:00","id":961136,"title":"","content":"Include a family of endron execs that are a wod version of the ewings from dallas, then have the pack be suspects in the &quot;who shot JR?&quot; craze even if they weren't involved (were there ever eco-terroists menacing the Ewings in that tv show?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T23:46:04-07:00","id":962133,"title":"","content":"Well I live in Oklahoma, next to Red River, so I go to Texas a lot. Texas is completely different from once side to the other. East Texas is forests and some swamps. While West Texas is scrub and desert. There is a....pond...cave lagoon...by san Antonio that Robert Rodriguez used in a movie...can't recall which one...that would make a interesting caern. Also by San Antonio is some natural caverns. They are a tourist attraction though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T00:29:10-07:00","id":962145,"title":"","content":"Saw Texas, logged in to comment. El Paso is the 19th largest city in the US, and both I-10 (Los Angeles to New Orleans) and I-25 (El Paso to Denver) pass through it; it's one of the largest shipping/transportation hubs in the US. Juarez (2 million metro) is a literal 20-minute walk over a bridge, and there's a huge military base (Ft. Bliss) and America's largest missle base (White Sands AFB) is 40-minutes away. The FBI has a building there, which also houses the ATF and Supreme Court. Asarco, which no longer has huge smokestacks there, is also a presence (and makes for good Pentex).<br /> <br /> Finally, in the 70s, it was estimated that 70% is all drugs that entered the US came in from El Paso. <br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T00:36:14-07:00","id":962150,"title":"","content":"Oh! And there's Waco Tanks, good climbing/hiking area, and Carlsbad Caverns, in New Mexico. And the third-largest city in New Mexico, Las Cruces, is less than an hour away. <br /> <br /> Outside of that, though, it's all trailer parks and scrub brush <br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T07:58:52-07:00","id":962286,"title":"","content":"If you want a western-like setting, I have to agree that El Paso is probably the way to go. It's out in the desert regions, but there are still mountains, plateaus, rivers, waterfalls (albeit small ones), and forested groves hidden throughout the landscape. Then you've also got the elements of there being no major cities for a hundred or more miles in any direction.<br /> <br /> You've also got a military base there (Fort Bliss) and you're right on the border of Mexico with Juarez on the other side (which I can't imagine has fared well in the World of Darkness).<br /> <br /> You could also consider Big Bend national park, located down in the 'elbow' of Texas. It's huge and would probably be a prime location for a Caern.<br /> <br /> If you want to step away from Desert and spaghetti western, most of North and Central Texas (anything east of the desert and west of the big cities on IH35 coming down the center-right of the state; or the entire &quot;panhandle&quot; at the top of the state) is where you're gonna find that small-town, good ole boy region. Country music, conservative people, bibles, football, and plains as far as the eye can see. Not too different from Kansas or Oklahoma... but don't tell them that.<br /> <br /> The IH35 corridor is where you've got your big cities (minus Houston). Dallas is sprawling and industrial. Dotting the highways that ring the city are smaller towns/cities that are considered part of the Metroplex though aren't Dallas/Fort Worth proper. Lots of industrial plants in this area as well, continuing down south to Waco.<br /> <br /> Further south is Fort Hood, one of the largest military bases in the US and a constant source of young infantry soldiers who like to make bad decisions in every city within driving distance.<br /> <br /> ---Nothing below this line will probably line up with the setting you're looking for---<br /> <br /> Keep going and you hit Austin, which is basically a county-sized chunk of California that somehow air-lifted into the center of a red state. Parks, hippies, hipsters, foodies, Bernie Sanders posters, computer companies and internet start ups. Half the city is somehow college students, despite having a couple million residents in the metroplex.<br /> <br /> Next you hit New Braunfels (and Canyon Lake to the West). Smaller town, with a big chunk of income coming from the massive water park and river/lake tourism. Lots of nice parks and nature areas around here, though you'd need some WoD tweaking to make anything private enough for a caern.<br /> <br /> After that is San Antonio- wide urban sprawl. Shorter buildings because land is cheap. Heavy hispanic influence but still unmistakably Texan. The Alamo is dead center in the city's downtown and a daily tourist attraction to hundreds. Again, you'd need some setting adjustments to use it for anything.<br /> <br /> The Urban line dead ends at Corpus Christi... aka fishing boats and SPRING BREAK! This might make an interesting setting, but again... nothing like the Preacher game you're looking for.<br /> <br /> As Mahjemm01 said, East of the corridor slowly turns from semi-urban hill country to a brief patch of tall forest, followed by a gradual transition to swamps and Louisiana. Houston and College Station (Texas A&amp;M university) are out in the middle of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12162,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","user":"Crusher-of-Cities","date":".  Fixed some typos 09-02-2016, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T17:05:12-07:00","id":962574,"title":"","content":"West Texas and the panhandle isn't much like Oklahoma. Far west Oklahoma is similar to west Texas. Around Amirillo is a lot of scrub and desert. And gentle hills. Might be worth mentioning that due to its collection near Texas, there is also a military base in Lawton, and Altas, Oklahoma. After you cross into Oklahoma the scrub starts giving way to prairie that leads in to forests. I don't have much knowledge of west Texas or south of Dallas. In East texas, after you pass Dallas the major urban areas (which to be honest aren't that major) is Long View, Tyler, Paris, Texarkana,Sherman/Denison, and then in Lousiana, Shreveport. Also right across Red River, all down its length, is Native American Casinos. Also, for flavor, if you want to venture into Oklahoma, Native Americans in OK do not have reservations. They have Nations. Like Choctaw Nation, Creek Nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","user":"Mahjemm01","date":". 09-02-2016, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T09:51:48-07:00","id":965016,"title":"","content":"i been thinking about the finale of my story (i DM by seasons like a tv show). and i been thinking about sending the pack to The Alamo (this one now being a caern) and them fighting fomori's and first team while trying to evac the kinfolks of the area, basically trying to do a retelling of the real Alamo battle. any suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T15:28:26-07:00","id":965298,"title":"","content":"Well, I'd take a walk around the Alamo with Google Maps.... it's the literal center of downtown San Antonio, much as a Capitol building or Mayor's office might be in other cities. Its neighbors include an IMAX theater, and a hotel with a shopping mall as its first few stories, and snaking around it and the rest of downtown is the Riverwalk (kind of a canal boardwalk) that includes bars open until 2am and the drunkards that stagger around after closing.<br /> <br /> So... you'll want to adjust the setting or provide a reason this battle can go somewhat unnoticed. Certainly a few city police are assigned to watch the monument at night as well to protect against vandalism.<br /> <br /> Size-wise the Alamo is surprisingly small. If you include all the outer walls, its footprint is probably smaller than most Walmarts.<br /> <br /> To make it happen, I'd set it around 3-4am, with some sort of supernatural power being used to drive the normals away. Maybe a Curse of Aeolus-type power to keep out the riffraff. After that, the Alamo would be the low-ground with numerous tall buildings and parking garages providing vantage over the park/monument... so the Garou could expect to be well pinned down while foot soldiers tried to cross the streets and plaza that lead up to the walls. Honestly... it'd probably make for a pretty exciting tactical challenge.<br /> <br /> Of course in the WoD, the Alamo and the lands around it might be home to no shortage of Wraiths as well... so maybe fewer high-end businesses would have decided to set up shop right next door. It's up to you how much your WoD differs from reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12162,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","user":"Crusher-of-Cities","date":".  Typos 09-07-2016, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T20:06:31-07:00","id":965443,"title":"","content":"If your going to use San Antonio and want the Alamo, a good movie that is set in San Antonio and part is in the Alamo is Cloak and Dagger. A 80s movie. Also I 35 isn't too far from downtown, so if you want a high speed chase/battle, there ya go. Just a little trivia for ya, in Christi Corpus they have a decom Aircraft Carrier harbored in port. Its basically a museum.<br /> <br /> Dallas is also a good city. There is a restaurant at top a...needle..tower...that has balls of light all around. Its in almost every pic of Dallas skyline. A battle in side that could be interesting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","user":"Mahjemm01","date":". 09-07-2016, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T21:26:12-07:00","id":965477,"title":"","content":"basically, im still writting down the details of the Season Ending (I like to DM stories as if they were a tv show)<br /> the players are slowly fighting and discovering the Fomori and what exactly are they or where do they come from, what i had in mind is that one of the players manages to tie Pentex to the Fomor through evidence, they go back to their sept (where their loved ones live) only to find that everyone is dead except one Kinfolk who's been helping them (a funny looking man who's last name sounds like HATE). i was thinking that, the kinfolk will tell the party that the First Team went to the sept, killed everyone and after they coudn't find the evidence , they took a hostage and they want an exchange in public. thats where The Alamo comes, thing is, The Alamo is a Sept but incredibly weak and most garou's there already gave up against the wyrm. The idea is basically that the pack of PC's figures that the First Team doesn't want the evidence, they want to tie all loose ends and that the pack will have to fight the intruders off while at the same time, learning what a Black Spiral Dancer Is...<br /> <br /> imma bend the rules a bit allowing the wraiths of The Alamo to help the Pc's while the first team will possibly involve the SWAT as a cheap tactic and then throw the real fire power, the idea is that PC's will Die during this battle","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T23:36:35-07:00","id":965521,"title":"","content":"Just south of San Antonio, right off I 35, is a cavern, tourist trap lol. Think Carlsbad, just smaller I believe. In my opinion , or at least what I would do, the Black Spirals have a Hive beneath San Antonio and the caves can be used for access to the Hive. Just a suggestion lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T23:54:53-07:00","id":965526,"title":"","content":"Hamilton Pool. 25 miles west of Austin. Was used as filming location in Predators. That was the place used by Robert Rodriguez that I mentioned in a earlier post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}